# C#/.NET security

Narrows `core-common-rules`' stack-agnostic security rules to C#/.NET-specific
risks (OWASP) and the safe framework API. Applies only to `*.cs` files.

## SQL and data access

- Parameterized queries for SQL from user-influenced input
  (`SqlCommand.Parameters.Add(...)`/`AddWithValue(...)` with `@`
  placeholders, EF Core LINQ, Dapper parameter objects); never
  `string.Format`/interpolation/concatenation into `CommandText`.
- An ORM's raw-SQL escape hatch (`FromSqlRaw`, Dapper raw string execution)
  takes user-influenced values as parameters; prefer `FromSqlInterpolated`
  over `FromSqlRaw` when the query needs any caller-supplied value.

## Deserialization of untrusted data

- Never `BinaryFormatter` on data not fully trusted (or at all on a current
  .NET version).
- Untrusted JSON through `System.Text.Json` with an explicit, known target
  type; no `TypeNameHandling.Auto`/`All` (`Newtonsoft.Json`) or custom
  `$type`-driven resolver.
- Allowlist any type passed to `XmlSerializer`/`DataContractSerializer` from
  untrusted input; do not resolve a type name from the payload.

## Secrets and configuration

- No hard-coded connection string, API key, or signing secret in source or
  `appsettings.json`; User Secrets (`dotnet user-secrets`) for local
  development, environment variables, Azure Key Vault, or the project's
  standard secret store beyond that.
- A connection string or secret read from `IConfiguration` comes from an
  environment-specific provider, not a value in `appsettings.json` or
  `appsettings.Development.json`.

## Path and file handling

- For an untrusted filename/segment, validate the resulting path stays under
  the intended root (`Path.GetFullPath` and a root-prefix check, or a
  filename allowlist) before `File.Open`/`File.ReadAllText`; `Path.Combine`
  alone does not stop `..`.

## Web and transport (ASP.NET Core)

- No `Html.Raw`/`@Html.Raw` on caller-supplied content outside Razor's
  default auto-encoding unless provably pre-sanitized.
- Never disable TLS certificate validation
  (`ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback` returning `true`
  unconditionally, including on `HttpClientHandler`) outside a short-lived
  local test, never shipped.
- Built-in antiforgery (`[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]`/`IAntiforgery`) for any
  state-changing endpoint reachable from a browser session; ASP.NET Core
  Identity/`PasswordHasher<TUser>` (or an equivalent vetted library) for
  password hashing, never a custom scheme.
